debian-minerva (0.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * "mana aluminiumnya" — the shell surface no longer depends on each base
    session's autostart implementation (xfce4-session skipped the autostart
    entry, so logins landed on a bare XFCE-grey desktop). minerva-session
    now starts minerva-shell-start DIRECTLY in every base branch (xfce,
    openbox, kiosk); the autostart .desktop is gone.
  * xfconf per-channel defaults (SaveOnExit=false, Super/Super+W/Ctrl+Alt+T/
    Super+E shortcuts) are written as plain XML before xfce4-session starts
    — no xfconf-daemon chicken-and-egg on first login.
  * minerva-shell-start slimmed to: token wait, browser pick, kiosk launch,
    respawn loop, loud self-check (report file + xmessage).

 -- Minerva Team <minerva@localhost>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:35:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WRAPPER BASE, by user directive: the session machinery is now delegated
    to proven Debian components instead of hand-rolled bootstrap.
    xfce4-session + xfwm4 run the session (window management, autostart,
    polkit, save-session); xfdesktop/xfce4-panel/xfce4-screensaver/
    xfce4-power-manager are masked via standard Hidden=true autostart
    overrides; the Minerva shell surface starts through XDG autostart
    (minerva-shell.desktop, OnlyShowIn=Minerva) like any other session app.
    openbox remains the fallback base, single kiosk window the last resort.
  * minerva-shell-start: launches the kiosk shell from autostart, applies
    idempotent xfconf shortcuts (Super = launcher, Super+W = overview,
    Ctrl+Alt+T = terminal, Super+E = files), and runs a loud self-check 8 s
    after start — any missing subsystem writes ~/minerva-report.txt AND
    pops an xmessage dialog, so a broken login can never be silent again.
  * enforcer kept (conditional geometry pin) and now WM-agnostic.
  * doctor: base-session checks (xfce4-session / xfwm4 / openbox).
  * shell: window.onerror surfaces a toast instead of dying quietly.
  * Depends: xfce4-session, xfwm4, xfconf; openbox moved to Recommends.

 -- Minerva Team <minerva@localhost>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:05:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.5.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enforcer no longer fights the window manager: the wmctrl geometry pin is
    applied only while the fullscreen state is missing (re-applying -e to an
    already-fullscreen window made openbox reconfigure the shell every tick
    — flicker and input stalls, i.e. "doesnt work at all").
  * Session writes a one-line ready file (mode, screen, pids, timestamp);
    minerva-doctor prints it plus a package-vs-web-assets version check so a
    half-upgraded install can never masquerade as a broken DE again.
  * Shell says out loud when a real session reports zero .desktop apps
    instead of silently showing a short launcher.

 -- Minerva Team <minerva@localhost>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:40:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.5.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * THE TOY-MODE KILLER. 0.5.5 exported MINERVA_SESSION_MODE *after* the
    daemon had already snapshotted its environment, so on every real VM the
    daemon ran in "dev" mode: exec/win_op refused, the shell fell back to its
    offline catalogue and the whole desktop behaved like a static mock-up
    ("UI cuman hiasan"). The mode + screen detection now runs before
    start_daemon, and the shell trusts any live Rust daemon that is not in
    kiosk mode, so real app launching / real dock mirroring can never be
    lost to an env-ordering accident again.
  * Shell surface can no longer float: the enforcer pins exact screen
    geometry via wmctrl -e on top of the fullscreen hint; chromium runs with
    --force-device-scale-factor=1 for deterministic VM pixel mapping.
  * minerva-doctor gains two evidence checks: daemon-vs-env session mode
    agreement, and shell window geometry vs the xrandr screen.
  * Battery icon on mains-only machines is a neutral full green instead of
    a red empty outline next to the AC pill.
  * Recommends open-vm-tools-desktop so VMware guests auto-fit resolution
    (black letterbox bars around the session were the guest keeping a small
    fixed resolution).

 -- Minerva Team <minerva@localhost>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:10:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.5.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 100-fix pass across the shell: bugfixes + one animation language
    (full numbered list in docs/FIXES-0.5.5.md). Highlights:
      - session polling no longer wipes the live EWMH window mirror
        (dock running indicators flickered every 2.5 s);
      - panel windows no longer consume the desktop's event queue;
      - west-edge window resize moves the left edge (was stretching
        the wrong way); drags stay on-screen; z-index rebase;
      - Quick Settings reachable again (power button opens it, its
        header button opens the power menu);
      - fabricated data removed: Task Manager CPU/RAM columns are now
        real load/memory, Displays reads real xrandr modes, the demo
        Mail inbox and the do-nothing Widgets picker are gone, icon
        artwork drops the Google brand palette, calendar art shows the
        real date;
      - battery pill reflects charge level (amber/red, AC on desktops
        without a battery) and refreshes from the daemon every minute;
      - API client: no leaked abort timers, empty-body safe, token on
        probe, 3-strike backend downgrade instead of one hiccup;
      - transitions/press feedback unified on every interactive
        surface; will-change scoped down; dead boot/setup/weather CSS
        removed; layers clear the 56 px dock.

