debian-minerva (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Shell windows (desktop/topbar/dock) now use a fresh chromium profile per
    login so window bounds saved by an earlier broken session can never be
    restored over the placement flags and Openbox rules.
  * Session checks that openbox is still alive right after start, retries
    once, and logs the outcome plus the per-window geometry it requested,
    so placement problems are diagnosable from session.log.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window placement fix: chromium honours --wm-class, not --class, so the
    Openbox application rules (topbar/dock/desktop/panels) never matched and
    every shell window fell back to a centred default-sized window. Panels
    and shell windows now set --wm-class (plus --class for compatibility),
    the rc.xml rules match both WM_CLASS instance and class, and the session
    passes explicit per-role --window-size/--window-position (and
    --start-fullscreen for the desktop) as a fallback.
  * Fix E0283 (ambiguous `.into()`) in the missing-token error response.
  * Drop dead Value::with() helper (build warning).

